6,A-Pucikwar language | Languages Wiki | Fandom,https://worldlanguages.fandom.com/wiki/A-Pucikwar_language,"A-Pucikwar or Pucikwar is a disputed extinct language spoken on the Andaman Islands of India, formerly spoken by the A-Pucikwar on the south coast on the Middle Andaman Island, the northeast coast of South Andaman Island, and on Baratang. As the colonization and settlement of the Andaman Islands increased from the late 19th century to the early 20th century, the indigenous Great Andamanese ...",A-Pucikwar,Andamanese
